true] [17592186444269 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444269 1071 "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444269 1072 #uuid "27db2f89-f211-5a22-8370-a36f3eeeed25" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444269 1074 "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $A$ and $B$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$A$  and $B$ only.\"" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444267 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1069 "q-35271" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1071 "If \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}]$, then $\\text{rank}(B)=$" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1072 #uuid "71b4ed44-551f-59fd-a0cd-dc5bcd55b071" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true] [17592186444270 1074 "To find the rank of $B,$ we first reduce it to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 12 & 18 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $2$ pivot columns (or alternatively, it has exactly $2$ non-zero rows).\n\nTherefore, $\\text{rank}(B)=2.$" 13194139534922 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-080f7b68-1446-53cb-a768-ddfed5710a59" 17592186444257 "answer-49a263fb-b924-566b-a1a2-e05321e1d5e8" 17592186444258 "answer-542dff14-ba5a-5094-8199-ab519cc9d8ce" 17592186444259 "answer-58ea38e8-5330-5713-ac69-29ba41df0ffb" 17592186444260 "answer-be020027-00e4-5988-94b8-3d6ef8dffe52" 17592186444261 "answer-d4a9245b-945c-5b2f-a3f2-23d524e7d6ca" 17592186444262 "answer-deeeee46-f112-5e27-a329-96e64bc24b65" 17592186444263 "answer-e0dfb5d5-ea82-565b-84e6-679186a0f012" 17592186444264 "answer-eb250ee6-15f1-5344-8651-c6fba9d86d91" 17592186444265 "answer-f29b74c5-893c-5a44-8e76-6c39f0301bb2" 17592186444266 "answer-field-2af22924-1cce-522c-aadc-abcfbbca5566" 17592186444267 "answer-field-b93d2a3e-8872-5847-9667-8c3c236eb8e4" 17592186444268 "question-27db2f89-f211-5a22-8370-a36f3eeeed25" 17592186444269 "question-71b4ed44-551f-59fd-a0cd-dc5bcd55b071" 17592186444270}}
